{"step_index":178,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T19:54:04Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-08-31T19:52:33Z sender=3a947e68-3423-4695-854c-73f678636de2 priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=I have drafted the Blender Python script that meets all the requirements (Domino chain reaction, rigid body physics, camera, lights, physics baking, and PNG sequence rendering). \n\nSince I am a read-only subagent, I cannot write files to the filesystem. Please use your `write_to_file` tool to save the following script to `C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\blender\\domino_sim.py`.\n\n```python\nimport bpy\nimport math\nimport os\n\ndef setup_domino_sim():\n    # Clear all existing mesh objects, cameras, and lights to start fresh\n    bpy.ops.object.select_all(action='SELECT')\n    bpy.ops.object.delete(use_global=False)\n    \n    scene = bpy.context.scene\n    \n    # Output settings\n    output_dir = os.path.join(\"C:\\\\Users\\\\renu5\\\\Downloads\\\\blender\", \"domino_render\")\n    if not os.path.exists(output_dir):\n        os.makedirs(output_dir)\n        \n    scene.render.filepath = os.path.join(output_dir, \"frame_\")\n    scene.render.image_settings.file_format = 'PNG'\n    scene.frame_start = 1\n    scene.frame_end = 150\n\n    # Ensure rigid body world exists\n    if not scene.rigidbody_world:\n        bpy.ops.rigidbody.world_add()\n\n    # 1. Ground Plane Setup\n    bpy.ops.mesh.primitive_plane_add(size=50, location=(0, 0, 0))\n    ground = bpy.context.active_object\n    ground.name = \"Ground\"\n    bpy.ops.rigidbody.object_add()\n    ground.rigid_body.type = 'PASSIVE'\n    ground.rigid_body.friction = 0.5\n\n    # 2. Domino Setup\n    # Dimensions (width, thickness, height)\n    dx, dy, dz = 0.4, 0.1, 1.0 \n    \n    # Create the master domino\n    bpy.ops.mesh.primitive_cube_add(size=1, location=(0, 0, dz/2))\n    domino = bpy.context.active_object\n    domino.scale = (dx, dy, dz)\n    domino.name = \"Domino\"\n    bpy.ops.object.transform_apply(location=False, rotation=False, scale=True)\n    \n    # Add Active Rigid Body to the master domino\n    bpy.ops.rigidbody.object_add()\n    domino.rigid_body.type = 'ACTIVE'\n    domino.rigid_body.mass = 0.1\n    domino.rigid_body.friction = 0.6\n    domino.rigid_body.restitution = 0.1\n    \n    # Create a chain of dominos\n    num_dominos = 25\n    spacing = 0.6\n    \n    for i in range(1, num_dominos):\n        # Position in a straight line\n        x = 0\n        y = i * spacing\n        z = dz / 2\n        \n        # Duplicate the master domino\n        bpy.ops.object.duplicate(linked=True)\n        new_domino = bpy.context.active_object\n        new_domino.location = (x, y, z)\n        \n    # Deselect all objects\n    bpy.ops.object.select_all(action='DESELECT')\n    \n    # Tilt the first domino to initiate the chain reaction\n    domino.select_set(True)\n    bpy.context.view_layer.objects.active = domino\n    # Rotate around X axis to make it fall towards the next domino\n    domino.rotation_euler = (math.radians(-20), 0, 0)\n    \n    # 3. Camera Setup\n    # Position the camera to view the entire chain\n    camera_y = (num_dominos * spacing) / 2\n    bpy.ops.object.camera_add(location=(8, camera_y, 6))\n    camera = bpy.context.active_object\n    camera.name = \"SimCamera\"\n    # Point the camera down and towards the dominos\n    camera.rotation_euler = (math.radians(60), 0, math.radians(90))\n    scene.camera = camera\n    \n    # 4. Lighting Setup\n    bpy.ops.object.light_add(type='SUN', location=(5, 5, 10))\n    sun = bpy.context.active_object\n    sun.data.energy = 3.0\n    sun.rotation_euler = (math.radians(45), math.radians(45), 0)\n    \n    # 5. Bake physics\n    # Set cache frame range\n    scene.rigidbody_world.point_cache.frame_start = 1\n    scene.rigidbody_world.point_cache.frame_end = scene.frame_end\n    \n    # Bake the cache\n    bpy.ops.ptcache.bake_all(bake=True)\n    \n    print(f\"Domino setup completed successfully. Renders will be saved to: {output_dir}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    setup_domino_sim()\n```\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
{"step_index":179,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T19:54:04Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-08-31T19:52:39Z sender=e5db259b-2ce0-4176-b477-0bb83c257e96 priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=I have generated the requested Python script for the Blender 5.2 Cloth Simulation. \n\nBecause I am a read-only subagent, I cannot modify your filesystem. Please use your `write_to_file` tool to save the following code to `C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\blender\\cloth_sim.py`.\n\n```python\nimport bpy\nimport math\n\ndef setup_scene():\n    # Clear existing scene\n    bpy.ops.object.select_all(action='SELECT')\n    bpy.ops.object.delete()\n\n    # 1. Create Pole\n    bpy.ops.mesh.primitive_cylinder_add(radius=0.1, depth=10, location=(0, 0, 5))\n    pole = bpy.context.active_object\n    pole.name = \"Pole\"\n    # Add collision so the flag doesn't pass through the pole\n    pole.modifiers.new(name=\"Collision\", type='COLLISION')\n\n    # 2. Create Flag (Cloth)\n    bpy.ops.mesh.primitive_grid_add(x_subdivisions=60, y_subdivisions=60, size=2, location=(2.1, 0, 9))\n    flag = bpy.context.active_object\n    flag.name = \"Flag\"\n    \n    # Rotate 90 degrees on X to stand it vertically\n    flag.rotation_euler = (math.radians(90), 0, 0)\n    bpy.ops.object.transform_apply(location=False, rotation=True, scale=False)\n    bpy.ops.object.shade_smooth()\n\n    # 3. Pinning (Left Edge)\n    vg = flag.vertex_groups.new(name=\"Pin\")\n    # Grid size is 2, local x goes from -1 to 1. Pin vertices on the far left.\n    pinned_verts = [v.index for v in flag.data.vertices if v.co.x < -0.95]\n    vg.add(pinned_verts, 1.0, 'ADD')\n\n    # 4. Cloth Modifier\n    cloth = flag.modifiers.new(name=\"Cloth\", type='CLOTH')\n    cloth.settings.vertex_group_mass = \"Pin\"\n    cloth.collision_settings.use_self_collision = True\n    \n    # Set cache duration\n    cloth.point_cache.frame_start = 1\n    cloth.point_cache.frame_end = 150\n\n    # 5. Wind Force Field\n    bpy.ops.object.effector_add(type='WIND', location=(-3, 0, 9), rotation=(0, math.radians(90), 0))\n    wind = bpy.context.active_object\n    wind.name = \"Wind\"\n    wind.field.strength = 1500\n    wind.field.noise = 5.0\n\n    # 6. Camera Setup\n    bpy.ops.object.camera_add(location=(2, -12, 9), rotation=(math.radians(90), 0, 0))\n    cam = bpy.context.active_object\n    bpy.context.scene.camera = cam\n\n    # 7. Light Setup\n    bpy.ops.object.light_add(type='SUN', location=(5, -5, 12), rotation=(math.radians(45), 0, math.radians(45)))\n    sun = bpy.context.active_object\n    sun.data.energy = 3.0\n\n    # 8. Setup Animation & Render Engine\n    bpy.context.scene.frame_start = 1\n    bpy.context.scene.frame_end = 150\n    \n    # Render Settings\n    render = bpy.context.scene.render\n    render.image_settings.file_format = 'PNG'\n    # Save PNG sequence to cloth_render directory (ensuring a trailing slash/backslash for directory rendering)\n    render.filepath = r\"C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\blender\\cloth_render\\\\\"\n    \n    # 9. Bake the Simulation\n    print(\"Baking cloth simulation...\")\n    bpy.ops.ptcache.bake_all(bake=True)\n    print(\"Bake complete! You can now render the animation sequence.\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    setup_scene()\n```\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
